    {
      "id": "claim_6d15383b291c4b68bb0b4319bcc0a05c",
      "statement": "CertificateFlow.Sign gets the client via GetClient, parses --not-before/--not-after and --template-data, builds api.SignRequest{CsrPEM, OTT, NotBefore, NotAfter, TemplateData}, calls client.Sign, falls back to ServerPEM+CaPEM when CertChainPEM is empty, serializes the chain to PEM, and writes the certificate file with mode 0o600.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L250-L293",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8654de214fa86c88ffdb297c7897329957a58767f3abf236bb47bc861c3ece08:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a66662866fb344ecae85ac655890d93a",
      "statement": "CreateSignRequest parses the OTT, derives key details from --kty/--curve/--size, generates the key, merges --san values with the token sans claim via splitSANs (dedupe + x509util.SplitSANs), applies per-token-type default SANs (AWS private IP + EC2 internal names, GCP project/zone internal names, Azure resource name, OIDC issuer#subject URI when subject equals the email, K8sSA uses the command-line subject, default uses the token subject), builds and signs a CSR with CommonName from the subject, verifies it with CheckSignature, and returns the SignRequest plus private key; DisableCustomSANs in the shared context suppresses appending the subject to cloud default SANs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L297-L421",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4783c16ba0274f978d91942ff7a609fadb18a0af5548a873a505a9c22efad2f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ec7cee599a0949a7b86af8d8eec8aa91",
      "statement": "OfflineCA wraps an authority.Authority and its config.Config from smallstep/certificates; NewOfflineCA is guarded by the offlineInstance singleton (double initialization is avoided because the badgerDB-backed authority holds locks), reads and unmarshals the --ca-config JSON, rejects configs without provisioners, applies --password-file, and calls authority.New.",
