      "id": "claim_ca5672f92905417ba37cdb4d425a0271",
      "statement": "bootstrap() validates the fingerprint by calling client.Root(fingerprint) on an insecure client; when UseContext is true it adds/sets the step context (authority and profile default to the context name), otherwise WarnContext prints a hint if a legacy config/ca.json exists; it writes the root PEM to pki.GetRootCAPath() with 0o600, writes bootstrapConfig (ca-url, fingerprint, root, optional redirect/provisioner/min-password-length) to step.DefaultsFile() with 0o644, sets ca-url/fingerprint/root on the CLI context, creates an empty profile defaults file when contexts are enabled, and with --install installs the root in the OS truststore.",
